get_started using C runtime API
Hi, I'm trying to run the get_started.py TVM function using the C runtime API but the program (listed below) segfaults when it makes the call to __tvm_main__/myadd. I'm guessing my invocation of TVMFuncCall is incorrect? For reference, everything is statically linked and gdb says that myadd is where it should be. This is the code that causes the error (extracted from c_runtime_api.cc): PackedFunc the_func = (*static_cast<const PackedFunc*>(func)); It doesn't even make it past the constructor. (Maybe constructing the FType goes wrong?). Thanks for any pointers [on fixing my pointers]! #include <stdlib.h> #include "runtime/c_runtime_api.h" int64_t shape[] = {3}; int64_t strides[] = {1}; extern void* __tvm_main__; TVMArray* mk_tensor(int8_t* data) { TVMArray *t = (TVMArray*)malloc(sizeof(TVMArray)); t->data = data; t->ndim = 1; t->shape = shape; t->strides = strides; t->byte_offset = 0; t->ctx.device_type = kDLCPU; t->ctx.device_id = 1; // int8 t->dtype.code = 0; t->dtype.bits = 8; t->dtype.lanes = 1; return t; } int main() { int8_t a_data[] = {1, 2, 3}; int8_t b_data[] = {2, 3, 4}; int8_t c_data[] = {0, 0, 0}; TVMValue arg_vals[3]; arg_vals[0].v_handle = mk_tensor(a_data); arg_vals[1].v_handle = mk_tensor(b_data); arg_vals[2].v_handle = mk_tensor(c_data); TVMValue ret_val; int ret_type_code; int arg_type_codes[] = {kArrayHandle, kArrayHandle, kArrayHandle}; TVMFuncCall(&__tvm_main__, arg_vals, arg_type_codes, 3, &ret_val, &ret_type_code); }
